    "body": "Probes features and fixes from the study branch. Subsumes #2321 and #2325 (now closed).\n\nCloses #2067\nCloses #2323\nCloses #2276\nCloses #2217\n\n## Features\n\n- **Drawer mode.** Expand a probe's sample into a multi-line, pretty-printed block below the code line (`Cmd/Ctrl+\u2193` open / `Cmd/Ctrl+\u2191` close, or the row's chevron; Esc exits). Per-probe state, capped at 15 rows (scrolls beyond). Built on a new `below` projector view slot reserving rows via `Tab(n)`.\n- **Enhanced Auto-probe** Auto-probe now probes top-level expressions as well ad defiitions. Auto-probe now has an `All` mode. Modes are `Off | Caret | All` (was on/off). _Caret_ probes the top-level definition under the cursor; _All_ probes the whole program, one probe per source row (a single root multiprobe). `Cmd/Ctrl+P` cycles Off\u2194All; the sidebar's segmented control also reaches Caret.\n- **\"Simple\" color scheme (new default).** Two colors: focal-call green vs. off-focus washed out green. replacing the old Hybrid default. Use the toggle in the sidebar to access the old default.\n\n## Fixes (pre-existing behavior)\n\n- **Probe samples no longer stale until the next edit:** Placing a probe (or autoprobe) showed the \u2205 indicator until the next edit, because the statics debounce left `probe_targets` stale and `IncrEval.reuse_check` reused a sampleless slice. Now a probe-id change forces a full statics refresh. (Also makes auto-probe work in exercise mode.)\n- **Step-into for indirect calls.** Extends the existing step-into to higher-order calls, partial applications, and `let f x = \u2026` sugar, by carrying a resolved call frame (`fn_def_id`) through evaluator state into each sample.\n- **More stable Sample-ids to prevent collisions on deep recursion** \u2014 fixes double-indication, twin resize handles, and broken scroll anchors via collision-resistant ids.\n- **Accurate Tab projector/refractor decoration offset** \u2014 Code/decoration row desync from out-of-order deferred-linebreak counting is fixed.\n- **Projector action index crash** \u2014 a stale render-time index now drops the action instead of raising.\n- Smaller: duplicate manual-refractor entry (assoc-list vs map disagreement), stuck pending probe cursor, a sibling-cleanup toggle that re-added forever, and pointer/drag guards.\n\n## Modifications / polish\n\n- **Sample-count indicator moved** from an overlay circle on the projector to an inline badge at the start of the samples row (hidden for a single sample).\n- **Sample dropdown now uses right-/alt-click.** The sample dropdown (which shows environment variables and pin/step options) opens on right-click or alt-click (was hover-only), with click-outside / scroll dismissal. Hover activation proved to hyperactive.\n- **Function-sugar probing.** Putting a multi-probe on `let f(args) = body` now probes the arguments on the header line, not just the body.\n- **Sample-focus navigation now scrolls horizontally:** When using \u2190/\u2192 move the focused sample it should scroll-follow it into view; this previously only worked vertically.\n- Indeterminant samples e.g. holes no longer colored differently than value samples; this proved confusing to multiple people.\n- Removed the dashed connector line between probes and samples; added visual noise doesn't pay for itself.\n- Sidebar quick-reference updated for new interactions (alt-click for env, right-click for pin/step, an expand-probe row).\n- Focus bar: \"Clear all\" also turns auto-probe off; the editor caret stays visible after a focus-bar / sidebar jump.\n- Scroll stability for drawer refractors: drawer-height changes above the caret are prevented from shifting it via scroll trigger.\n- Tuple pretty-printing breaks symmetrically\n- The test pass/fail badge no longer floats above probe sample menu.\n\n## Performance\n\n- Viewport culling now re-enabled, but only for auto-probe All mode (infra already existed on dev but was inert): off-screen probe views are culled in the single-editor modes (Scratch / Documentation / Tutorial); Exercises stays unculled.\n- Cull-before-build for probe views, memoized multi-probe expansion + placeholder calcs, and phys-equality gating on rebuilds.\n\n## Late additions: cards + rich-view UX (2026-08-22)\n\n- Cherry-picks Alexander's card RichProbe renderer (authorship preserved) (from `card-rich-probe`), forward-ported to this branch's registry API (`empty`, `drawer_rows`), with card/hand shape-matching intact.\n- Rich views render **inside** the sample chip (green backing, inert content) rather than replacing the row \u2014 the chip keeps the dropdown (Hide), sample capture, dbl-click, and resize. The anchored modal is retired: small rich views (\u22644 rows) embed in the row; taller ones auto-open the drawer on activation. Many mode shows one card/fan per sample.\n- **Rich Views** toggle in the probes sidebar (default on): probes auto-render the first applicable renderer when it fits; double-click flips an individual probe back to text. Tables remain opt-in.\n- Empty hands render a card-footprint silhouette (dotted outline, \u2205) instead of nothing.\n- Offside **stagger**: an after-display pass floors each display at the end of every code line it spans and first-fits it among displays from rows above, so multi-row content (card fans) overlaps neither program text nor other probes.\n",
